# Always Use Quickmerge

RULE: ALWAYS run `bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "message"`. NEVER run `scripts/quality-gates.sh` standalone. Use `--dep-branch` when dependencies differ from main. Branch protection rejects direct push to main.
WHY: Quickmerge runs dependency cascade, pre-flight audit, quality gates, Act simulation, and PR creation. Standalone quality gates miss critical checks.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/feature-branch-workflow.md, 06-coding-standards/quality-gates.md

## Branch / Staging Model

| Branch type | Quickmerge command | Effect |
|-------------|-------------------|--------|
| `feat/*` or `feature/*` | `bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "feat: ..." --no-pr` | QG only — no PR, branch stays open |
| `staging` | `bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "feat: ..."` | QG + auto-PR to main |
| Direct on `main` | blocked by branch protection | — |

**Auto-PR detection:** quickmerge auto-adds `--no-pr` when current branch starts with `feat/` or `feature/`.
To promote to main: merge feature into staging → run quickmerge on staging.

## Dependency Cascade (--dep-branch)

When `--dep-branch NAME` is set and a dependency has local changes, quickmerge **automatically cascades** into that dependency repo (in topological order, T0 first) and runs quickmerge there with the same branch name and flags.

This means ONE quickmerge call propagates T0 → T1 → T2 → T3 → Service in order.

```bash
# On unified-trading-library (T1), with changes also in unified-config-interface (T0):
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "feat: ConfigReloader extraction" --dep-branch "feat/config-reloader"
# Stage 1 detects UCI has changes → cascades into UCI first
# UCI quickmerge runs → pushes feat/config-reloader branch to UCI remote
# Then UTS quickmerge continues, installs UCI from local path dep (already updated)
```

Local changes are ALWAYS preserved through cascade — stash/pop mechanism ensures nothing is lost.

## Two-Step Quickmerge Workflow (per tier)

```
quickmerge --unit-only    → fast feedback: lint + type + unit tests only
                            catches critical import errors, syntax, obvious breaks
                            CI integration tests may still fail — that is expected
                            fix critical issues, then →

quickmerge (full)         → complete validation: all tests + act simulation
                            tier is "green" only when this passes
```

## Flags

```bash
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "feat: add feature"
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "feat: add feature" --unit-only          # fast: lint+type+unit only, skip integration+act
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "feat: add feature" --no-pr              # QG only, no PR (feature branches)
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "feat: add feature" --dep-branch "feat/X" # branch isolation + cascade
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "feat: add feature" --quick              # skip act simulation only
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "feat: add feature" --skip-tests         # lint+type only (no tests at all)
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "feat: add feature" --files "a.py b.py"  # multi-agent: stage only these files
```

## DO

```bash
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "feat: add ConfigReloader"
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "fix: tier boundary" --dep-branch "feat/rollback"
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "chore: cleanup" --no-pr                 # check locally without PR
```

## NEVER

```bash
bash scripts/quality-gates.sh                   # standalone — misses dep validation + PR
git add -A && git commit && git push            # bypasses all quality gates
git reset --hard origin/main                    # FORBIDDEN — destroys local changes
Finish with uncommitted changes in any modified repo
```

## Nothing-to-Commit on Staging

If staging branch has no new commits beyond main (everything worked first time):
```bash
git commit --allow-empty -m "chore: promote feat/X to staging"
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "chore: promote feat/X to staging"
```
Or simply let the merge commit from `git merge feature/X` onto staging be the trigger.
